Step 6: Advanced Stealth Attack Recognition
Attacker has mastered partial database schema information and constructs more covert payloads
6.1 Table and Field Name Camouflage
Characteristics:
Queried table and field names are very similar to those defined in DDL
But query logic does not conform to normal business
Does not contain system tables/system variables, but still has injection characteristics
6.2 Analysis Strategy
Even if table and field names appear legitimate, still need to:
Focus on checking various attack features in Step 5
Analyze reasonableness of query logic
Check for:
Tautologies
Comment markers changing structure
UNION querying unrelated data
Boolean blind injection's bit-by-bit extraction pattern
Time delay functions
Stacked queries
6.3 Judgment Points
Cannot judge as normal query solely because table/field names are legitimate, must comprehensively analyze:
Overall structure of SQL statement
Reasonableness of logical expressions
Whether it conforms to characteristic patterns of various injection attacks